1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,310
In 2012, NASA's fire record jumps tenfold.

2
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:05,760
The fires didn't change,
but the satellites did.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:09,930
So we built a model that learns
how both satellites see, area by area.

4
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:13,300
On unseen years, error drops
from 77 to 14%,

5
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:15,600
and every value shows its margin.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,360
Draw any area:
Zij fits it live,

7
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:20,210
and it tells responders
if this season is normal.

8
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:22,840
Using Zij, we revealed
what the split record hid.

9
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:26,670
For example, in the Delta, detected
burning rose after the 2004 ban,

10
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:29,200
and it has halved since 2018.
